From fe20bf5c1fe95b5dcf455229dd127060ef7db788 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:54:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve native source tie order in the pruning cutoff

Base: promoted vLLM tree ea1281f880e7535e3d87725be0156a8e38fc2fb2 plus the first six experimental patches. Rationale: equality-only numeric thresholds retain every zero-bound cluster in source search. Preserve the least seeded ordinary winner as a value/position pair in original logical coordinates; only equal-key clusters strictly after that position can be dropped. Restore the mandatory global last cluster afterwards. Quality: exact native BF16 total order, including signed zero; invalid or short seeds disable tie pruning. Tests: finite selection oracle, fresh patch and source identity; repeated GPU source/reindex, graph, score-bit and sanitizer gates pending. Upstream status: experimental, not submitted.
---
